Structural Check
- [S1] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `['Yes']`. | Variable `v2` has an invalid range `['Yes']`.
- [S2] STC15 failed: Every variable used in a guard must be formally defined. | Guard `v1 = 'Yes'` on `b1 -> n2` uses undefined variable `v1`. | Guard `v2 = 'Yes'` on `b1 -> n3` uses undefined variable `v2`. | DSL: guard(b1,n2,"v1 = 'Yes'"); guard(b1,n3,"v2 = 'Yes'")

Logical Sanity Check
- [L1] LSC1 failed: Every guard must be satisfiable under the declared ranges of its referenced variables. | Guard `v1 = 'Yes'` on `b1 -> n2` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Guard `v2 = 'Yes'` on `b1 -> n3` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range. | DSL: guard(b1,n2,"v1 = 'Yes'"); guard(b1,n3,"v2 = 'Yes'")
